WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.220 --> 00:00:04.320
These lanky insects are called assassin bugs

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:06.330
– and rightfully so

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:08.820
They ambush their dinner by

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:10.820
sneaking up on spiders in their own webs

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:14.380
The assassin bug often slices through strands

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:17.420
to take the most direct path to its prey,

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:20.220
but scientists were stumped

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:24.400
Now, a new study reveals how assassin bugs

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.580
limit telltale vibrations

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:29.600
Assassin bugs slowly grasp strands of web

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:31.460
with their foretarsi,

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:33.980
carefully pull them away from each other

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:35.520
until they break,

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.000
Then they gently release the ends to minimize

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.940
any vibrations the spider might feel

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:43.680
Researchers used laser vibrometry to measure

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:46.640
the vibrations caused by this maneuver,

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.940
and they were virtually undetectable—

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:51.820
revealing how these bugs earned their name

